<h2 id="trace-section-filtered-derived-functors" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="03TC">64.8</span> Filtered derived functors</h2>

<p>
And then there are the filtered derived functors. 
</p>
<p>
<article class="env-definition" id="03TD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03TD">Definition <span data-tag="03TD">64.8.1</span>.</a> Let $T: \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ be a left exact functor and assume that $\mathcal{A}$ has enough injectives. Define $RT: DF^+(\mathcal{A}) \to D F^+(\mathcal{B})$ to fit in the diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ DF^+(\mathcal{A}) \ar[r]^{RT} &  DF^+(\mathcal{B}) \\  K^+(\mathcal{I}) \ar[u] \ar[r]^{T \quad } &  K^+(\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{B})). \ar[u]}  \]
</div>
  <p> This is well-defined by the previous lemma. Let $G: \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ be a right exact functor and assume that $\mathcal{A}$ has enough projectives. Define $LG: DF^-(\mathcal{A}) \to DF^-(\mathcal{B})$ to fit in the diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ DF^-(\mathcal{A}) \ar[r]^{LG} &  DF^-(\mathcal{B}) \\  K^-(\mathcal{P}) \ar[u] \ar[r]^{G \quad } &  K^-(\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{B})). \ar[u]}  \]
</div>
  <p> Again, this is well-defined by the previous lemma. The functors $RT$, resp. $LG$, are called the <em>filtered derived functor</em> of $T$, resp. $G$. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<p>
<article class="env-proposition" id="03TE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03TE">Proposition <span data-tag="03TE">64.8.2</span>.</a> In the situation above, we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{gr}^ p \circ RT = RT \circ \text{gr}^ p  \]
</div>
  <p> where the $RT$ on the left is the filtered derived functor while the one on the right is the total derived functor. That is, there is a commuting diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ DF^+(\mathcal{A}) \ar[r]^{RT} \ar[d]_{\text{gr}^ p} &  DF^+(\mathcal{B}) \ar[d]^{\text{gr}^ p}\\  D^+(\mathcal{A}) \ar[r]^{RT} &  D^+(\mathcal{B}).}  \]
</div>
</article> 
</p>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>
<p>
Given $K^\bullet \in DF^+(\mathcal{B})$, we get a spectral sequence 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  E_1^{p, q} = H^{p+q}(\text{gr}^ p K^\bullet ) \Rightarrow H^{p+q}(\text{forget filt}(K^\bullet )).  \]
</div>
